message: "If you use the methods or implementation presented in this repository, please cite the associated research paper once published."
type: software
title: "DPP-Prov-Ver: Temporal Provenance, Causal Versioning, and Conflict Resolution for Digital Product Passports"
authors:
  - family-names: Miron
    given-names: Radu
    affiliation: "Technical University of Cluj-Napoca"
abstract: >-
  Research prototype built on Hyperledger Fabric for temporal component
  provenance, causal lifecycle versioning, semantic conflict detection,
  conflict resolution, and historical corrections in distributed Digital
  Product Passports.
keywords:
  - digital product passport
  - Hyperledger Fabric
  - temporal provenance
  - vector clocks
  - conflict resolution
  - blockchain
